  "worked_solution": "The level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ {e}^{4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-z-3} & =c \\\\ 4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-z-3 & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061c \\\\ z & =4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-3-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061c,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c>0.$\n\nTherefore, we get a family of elliptic paraboloids:\n\n$$\nz=4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}-3-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061c,\\,c\\in (0,\\infty )\n$$",
